d3d11: pow2 partitioning is integer partitioning in the tessellator

Applies on top of 0014.

The tessellator rounded every pow2 factor up to a power of two.  WARP's
pow2 output is byte-identical to its integer output (d3d11-so-probe:
triangles with factors 1..6, quads 1..5): the fixed-function tessellator
places pow2 points like integer partitioning, and rounding to a power of
two is left to the hull shader (the ProcessTessFactors helpers).  With the
rounding, every non-power-of-two pow2 factor was tessellated denser than
on Windows (tri-pow2 150 primitives, WARP 97; quad-pow2 47, WARP 38),
which images of flat patches did not show.

The tessellation vertex-hull variant digest of pow2 hull shaders takes a
constant, so conversions cached by an earlier build are not replayed;
every other partitioning keeps its cache entries.

--- a/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal
+++ b/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal
@@ -107,9 +107,13 @@
 template <>
 fxp32
 regularize_factor<partitioning::pow2>(float factor) {
-  // For pow2 partitioning, TessFactor range is [1,2,4,8,16,32,64].
-  uint clamped = clamp(ceil(factor), 1.0f, 64.0f);
-  return (clamped == 1 ? 1 : 1 << (32 - clz(clamped - 1))) << 16;
+  // AnyOS: the fixed-function tessellator treats pow2 partitioning as
+  // integer partitioning (WARP's pow2 output is byte-identical to its
+  // integer output for factors 1..6); rounding a factor up to a power of two
+  // is the hull shader's business (the ProcessTessFactors helpers), not the
+  // tessellator's.  Rounding here as well made every non-power-of-two factor
+  // denser than on Windows (d3d11-so-probe tri-pow2: 150 primitives, WARP 97).
+  return ((uint)clamp(ceil(factor), 1.0f, 64.0f)) << 16;
 }
 
 template <>
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_shader.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_shader.cpp
@@ -242,6 +242,11 @@
   h.update(variant.max_potential_tess_factor);
   if (variant.input_layout_handle)
     h.update(variant.input_layout_handle->sha1());
+  // AnyOS: pow2 partitioning places points like integer partitioning since
+  // 0015; conversions cached before it are not replayed (only pow2 hull
+  // shaders change, D3D11_SB_TESSELLATOR_PARTITIONING_POW2 = 2).
+  if (shader->reflection().Tessellator.Partition == 2)
+    h.update(uint32_t(0x4f720015));
   auto variant_digest = h.final();
   std::string func_name = "vshs_" + shader->sha1().string().substr(0, 8) + "_" + variant_digest.string() + "_a" + std::to_string(AIRCONV_VERSION);
   auto proc = [=](const char *func_name, SM50_SHADER_COMMON_DATA *common) -> sm50_bitcode_t  {
